<title>UK: Volvos elude thieves - Eagle Star.</title>
<headline>Volvos elude thieves - Eagle Star.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volvos are the least likely car to be stolen in the UK, insurer Eagle Star said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Eagle Star, the mainly general insurance subsidiary of B.A.T, said in a statement that Nissans, Jaguars, Renaults and Mercedes also fared well in its survey of cars and crime.</p>
<p>&quot;For makers such as Volvo and Nissan we have already been able to cut premiums,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>Volvos suffered a crime rate of just 0.7 percent a year, compared with 2.3 percent for Fords.</p>
<p>High performance cars are the most likely to be stolen or broken into, while all cars are more vulnerable when new, the survey found.</p>
<p>Eagle Star based its findings on recent claims made by its 800,000 motor insurance customers.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Insurance News 44 171 542 2769</p>
